# A Turing machine, simulated: the rewriter's Turing-completeness argument made
# executable. State and head position live in the tape, and one rule encodes
# one transition.
#
#   run: rw progs/tm.rw '<A>'
#
# Tape is bracketed by < and >. The head marker (A/B/C) sits immediately left
# of the cell being read, so a transition is a purely local rewrite:
#
#   write t, move R, go to Q :   "Xs -> tQ"
#   write t, move L, go to Q :   "xXs -> Qxt"   (one rule per cell value x)
#
# The machine is the 3-state busy beaver champion, 1RB1RH_0RC1RB_1LC1LA: from
# a blank tape it halts after 14 steps having written six 1s. Halting is free
# -- no rule mentions H, so once the head becomes H nothing matches and the
# rewriter stops on its own.

# blank supply: the tape is only ever as long as it has needed to be
A>->A0>
B>->B0>
C>->C0>
<A-><0A
<B-><0B
<C-><0C

# A: 0 -> 1,R,B    1 -> 1,R,H
A0->1B
A1->1H

# B: 0 -> 0,R,C    1 -> 1,R,B
B0->0C
B1->1B

# C: 0 -> 1,L,C    1 -> 1,L,A
0C0->C01
1C0->C11
0C1->A01
1C1->A11
